dialogue trust_barbarian_5
title: The white cloth
trigger: Trust barbarian level=5
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Barbarian fought the whole battle today without once losing the count. Now they sit by the fire, unwinding the old white strip from their knuckles for the last time.
  * I didn't have to shout the word once today. -> word_kept
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_word
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * You fought hot today, and you never lost the count. I said I'd rather have the anger. I still would. -> trusted_kept
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_trusted
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * You haven't sat a fight out since I said that. Not one. -> leash_kept
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_leashed
    do: AddTrust $with 6
  * You were quiet out there today. -> quiet
    do: AddTrust $with 3

node word_kept hero
  No. I heard it anyway, in my own head. Saltmoss. Turns out once you know who it's for, you don't need it shouted.
  -> red

node trusted_kept hero
  You said you'd rather have it. I've been holding you to that a long while. You never once took it back.
  -> red

node leash_kept hero
  I hated you a little for that, back then. Then I watched you mean it about everyone, not just me. So I learned to stay.
  -> red

node quiet hero
  Quiet. Aye, it was. Strange thing to be, after all these years.
  -> red

node red hero
  The red's still there, Commander. I'd not lie to you about that. It just knows whose side it's on now.
  -> brother

node brother commander
  The fire pops. In the Barbarian's other hand, the old tithe token turns once, then lies still.
  * We said we'd go back for your brother. That still stands, whatever comes. -> home
    if: FlagSet barbarian:tithe_home
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian:thread_home
  * We said the Choir would answer for him. I haven't forgotten. -> avenge
    if: FlagSet barbarian:tithe_avenge
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian:thread_avenged
  * I told you once it would carry you off one day. I was wrong about you. -> wrong
    if: FlagSet barbarian:tithe_warned
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian:thread_wrong
  * Tell me about your brother. Not the tithe. Him. -> him
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian:thread_him

node home hero
  I learned to read the marks on his token. Took me most of a month. There's more of him left than I feared. Enough to come home to.
  -> gift

node avenge hero
  Nor have I. But when it comes, I'll be standing beside you, not out ahead swinging. That's the difference now.
  -> gift

node wrong hero
  You weren't wrong, not then. You were just early. I needed someone to say it, so I'd have something to prove.
  -> gift

node him hero
  He hummed to the goats, off-key, every one a different song. Called the old nanny "Captain" because she bit. I've not said his name aloud in years. It was Ash. There. Now someone else knows.
  -> gift

node gift hero
  Here. The white cloth off the tithe wagon. It's carried every cut since the first night. I'd like you to have it, if you'll take it.
  -> last

node last commander
  The strip is grey with old blood and soft from washing, and lighter than it looks.
  * I'll carry it. All the way to the end of this. -> carry
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag barbarian:cloth_carried
  * Keep it. Your hands need it more than mine do. -> keep
    do: AddTrust $with -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian:cloth_kept
  * Tie it round my wrist, then take the first watch tonight. Like at the ford. -> watch
    if: FlagSet founding:watch_barbarian
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag barbarian:cloth_carried

node carry hero
  Then that's settled. Wherever you go, I go, and the red goes with me. On your side, Commander. Always on your side.

node keep hero
  Fair. Stubborn, but fair. I'll keep it, then, and you'll know where to find it. On the hand that's swinging for you.

node watch hero
  Ha. Hold still, then. There. Get some sleep, Commander. Nothing comes near this fire without going through me first.
